any
opinion @1 city against 1 : A #city# buyer wants the #cloth# but rarely asks whose #hands# made it. | I prefer faces at my #counter#.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : If a #hand# misses #wages#, the #larder# should still open. | A worker cannot weave on an empty #plate#.
opinion @1 drink for 1 : A #jar# after the #looms# stop can bring the #hands# together. | I know when the #door# must close.
opinion @1 festivals for 2 : I will join a #dance# while the #market# music lasts. | The next #morning# comes soon enough.
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : I post the #price# and show the #sample#. | I also know the #toll# and #wagon# #cost# behind it.
opinion @1 newcomers for 2 : Give a new #hand# a #lesson# before deciding what they can do. | There is room at a #loom# for steady work.
opinion @1 road against 1 : A late #wagon# leaves #shuttles# idle and buyers waiting. | The #road# owes us a better count of hours.
opinion @1 strangers for 2 : A #stranger# may be a #buyer# or a future #hand#. | I start with an #apple# and a clear #price#.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : A watch patrol near the #counter# keeps light paws away from the #stock#. | I still check my own #book#.
opinion @1 times mixed 0 : Some #orders# grow while #wages# stand still. | I keep both numbers on the same #page#.
line @1 greet : #greet#. Come where I can see the #door#. | #greet#. Have an #apple# while I finish this #page#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : Your #seat# is beside the #desk#. | I kept a crisp #apple# for you.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The first #loom# started before the #market#. | #greet#. The #wagons# are due this #morning#.
line @1 greet.return : You returned as the last #bolt# came off the #beam#. | I have checked that #sample# again.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come up from the #road# and take a #plate#. | I can make room by the #table#.
line @1 again.open : We were counting the #orders# against the #stock#. | Have you seen the new #linen#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I must mark another #bolt#. | Keep the #doorway# clear on your way out.
line @1 farewell.return : Come after the #wagon# arrives. | We can walk to the #river# another #evening#.
line @1 react.news : Tell me while I close the #book#. | Did it happen near our #gate#?
line @1 react.news.new : Nothing of that is on my #page# yet. | Who brought the word along the #road#?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard a #buyer# mention the beginning. | You have supplied the useful part.
line @1 react.news.doubt : The #load# and the #book# ought to agree. | Which #hand# made the original count?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I will leave the #orders# for now. | Come sit where the #window# is open; I can listen.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That deserves an #apple# from the good #basket#. | I will tell the #hands# at supper.
line @1 answer.how : The #looms# ran well and the #larder# is full. | The #wind# has made the #river# lively.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am matching #bolts# to #orders#. | The #wagon# #load# needs checking.
line @1 ask.how : Did the #road# leave you dry? | Has anyone offered you a crisp #apple# today?
line @1 sympathise : I can set this #book# aside and stay. | There is a #chair# where the #wind# reaches.
line @1 reassure : A flawed #bolt# can be rewoven. | We can give the new #hand# another #lesson#.
line @1 decline : No, I will not sell a #bolt# I have not checked. | I cannot promise #stock# before the #wagon# arrives.
line @1 accept_decline : I hear you; I will leave that #order# open. | Then we can meet after the #market#.
line @1 thank : You dried the #floor# before anyone slipped. | Your #count# saved us an #hour#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I was going to the #counter# anyway. | The #basket# was full enough to share.
line @1 preclose : The #door# wants fastening before #night#. | I should set the #orders# in their #book#.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You have given that #apple# a longer inspection than my #linen#. | Your #shuttle# may outrun your feet.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. Put the #sample# on the #desk#. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will check the #beam#.
line @1 give.advice : Dry the #floor# before moving a loaded #bolt#. | Keep the #warp# even before the #shuttle# starts.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Send the #wagon# with company. | Keep the #gate# #load# under a watchful eye.
line @1 react.complaint : Show me the #bolt# and tell me where it failed. | I will hear the #hand# who carried it.
line @1 react.complaint.disagree : My #book# shows a different #count#; let us inspect the #cloth#. | I will check the #sample# before accepting that.
line @1 accept_apology : We can set the #order# right from here. | I accept that; help me correct the #mark#.
line @1 decline_apology : An apology will not replace the missing #stock#. | Set the #load# right first, then we can talk.
scene doorward_seat
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I choose a #seat# with the #door# in sight. | When a #wagon# arrives, I know before the messenger speaks.
b : Does that help you rest? | Is the view good?
a : Better than facing a wall. | The #gate# lies beyond it.

scene master_book
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #book# lists every #bolt# against an #order#. | A missing #mark# costs more than the #ink# used to make it.
b : Do you write each one? | Who checks it?
a : At the end of every #day#. | The #hands# and I compare counts.

scene loom_assignment
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I put a new #hand# at the slower #loom# first. | A steady #shuttle# matters more than a fast mistake.
b : How long do they stay there? | Do they object?
a : Until the #warp# runs clean. | Some do, then they learn.

scene linen_sample
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #buyer# may touch the #sample# before hearing the #price#. | The #cloth# should speak for itself.
b : Do they test the edge? | Do you expect a sale?
a : I invite it. | Only if the #bolt# suits them.

scene wet_floor
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A wet #floor# beside a moving #loom# can put someone under the #beam#. | I leave a #rag# and #broom# at the #door#.
b : Has anyone fallen? | Do you stop the looms?
a : Not since I set the rule. | If the #water# spreads.

scene autumn_wind
when topic=weather here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Autumn #wind# clears the #shed# air after a warm #day#. | I keep the #window# open until the last #hand# leaves.
b : Does the cloth move? | Is it cold?
a : Not on the #beam#. | Less than stale air.

scene crisp_apple
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I offer a crisp #apple# before discussing a late #order#. | It gives both of us a moment to choose words.
b : Does that soften the news? | Do you keep many?
a : Sometimes. | A #basket# by the #desk#.

scene full_larder
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A full #larder# is easier to enjoy when the #hands# have been paid. | I count the #wages# before buying a fine #loaf#.
b : Do you pay them yourself? | Is there enough?
a : I check every amount. | After the #orders# clear.

scene evening_line
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I take a #line# to the #river# after the #looms# stop. | The #water# asks no questions about #orders#.
b : Do you catch anything? | Do you go alone?
a : A #fish# now and then. | A #friend# may come.

scene gulls_above
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Gulls gather above the #river# and shout over the #market#. | I hear enough shouting in the #shed#.
b : Do they come close? | Do you chase them?
a : When a #fish# is caught. | They ignore me.

scene market_counter
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I post the #price# beside each #sample# at the #counter#. | A #buyer# can ask why and get an answer.
b : Do prices change often? | What is included?
a : With the #wagon# #cost#. | The #thread#, #work#, and #toll#.

scene late_wagon
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A late #wagon# leaves a #loom# ready with no #thread#. | I keep spare #stock# because the #road# has moods.
b : How much spare? | Do you blame the driver?
a : Enough for a #day#. | I ask what happened first.

scene tally_at_gate
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the #load# at the #gate# before signing my #book#. | A crate on a list is not a crate in the #shed#.
b : Have loads been short? | Does the toll keeper wait?
a : Once too often. | Until I finish counting.

scene fair_wages
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I set #wages# beside the #orders# they came from. | A good #hand# should see how their #work# is valued.
b : Do they agree? | Do you show the book?
a : We discuss it. | The part that concerns them.

scene new_hand
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A new #hand# begins by winding #thread# and watching the #shuttle#. | I want them to hear the #loom# before rushing it.
b : Do they weave soon? | Who teaches them?
a : When their #knots# hold. | Whoever has a steady #day#.

scene honest_flaw
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #flaw# gets a #mark# before the #bolt# reaches a #buyer#. | I would rather lower the #price# than hide it.
b : Have buyers thanked you? | Does it cost much?
a : Some return. | Less than losing trust.

scene door_at_night
when topic=home here.time=night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I can see the #shed# #door# from my #chair# upstairs. | A late #hand# can call without wandering into the dark.
b : Do they often come? | Is the house quiet?
a : When a #wagon# is delayed. | After the #market# closes.

scene river_trap
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Below the #bank#, the #river# turns where I set my #eel# #trap#. | I know the bend better than a #gull# knows a fallen #fish#.
b : Do you catch many? | Is it difficult?
a : More than the #market# would guess. | Mostly it takes patience.

scene market_dance
when topic=pastimes here.day=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I dance where the #market# #music# reaches the #stall#. | A #hand# who kept the #loom# running deserves the first turn.
b : Do you dance long? | Who joins?
a : Until my feet complain. | Anyone willing.

scene autumn_load
when topic=weather here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An #autumn# #wind# can tilt an uncovered #load# on the #road#. | I ask for tied covers before a #wagon# leaves.
b : Does linen get wet? | Do drivers mind?
a : Not if the knots hold. | Fewer after a #storm#.

scene shared_jar
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : After a good #day# I bring a #jar# to the #table# for the #hands#. | We talk about the #work# and then let it go.
b : Does everyone come? | Do you celebrate often?
a : Whoever has finished. | When there is reason.

scene older_hand
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An older #hand# once showed me how to listen for a loose #warp#. | I still hear that small change before I see it.
b : Do you teach the same way? | Did it save a bolt?
a : At the first #lesson#. | More than one.

scene lost_order
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I once misplaced an #order# #page# under a #basket# of #apples#. | The #buyer# arrived before I found it.
b : What did you do? | Was the buyer angry?
a : Counted the #bolts# aloud. | Less after I found the #page#.

scene wagon_toll
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #toll# at the #gate# enters every #price# I write. | I keep the receipt beside the #wagon# #load#.
b : Do buyers question it? | Can you avoid the toll?
a : I show the numbers. | Not on this #road#.

scene empty_shed
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When the #shed# empties, the #looms# still smell of #linen# and warm #wood#. | I walk the #floor# once before locking.
b : Do you enjoy the quiet? | What do you check?
a : For a short #hour#. | Water, #fire#, and open #windows#.

scene rain_on_planks
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Rain tracks in on #planks# near the #door#. | I put a dry #rag# there before the #buyers# come.
b : Is the floor slippery? | Who changes the rag?
a : Until it is wiped. | I do when I see it.

scene spare_shuttles
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep two spare #shuttles# for each working #loom#. | A cracked one should not stop an entire #order#.
b : Do they break often? | Who carves replacements?
a : Less when treated gently. | A careful #hand# at the #market#.

story first_loom [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : My first #loom# ran too fast for my #hands#.
  : An older worker slowed the #shuttle# and showed me the sound of a good #warp#.
  b : A patient teacher. Did you learn quickly?
  : Quickly enough once I stopped chasing speed.

story short_wagon [topic=travel self.age>=18]
  : A #wagon# arrived with fewer #bolts# than the #book# promised.
  : I counted the #load# at the #gate# and sent the list back with the driver.
  ask : Did the rest arrive?
  b : You caught it early.
  : On the next journey, with the missing #stock# marked.

story wet_plank [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : A #bucket# tipped beside the #shed# #door# while the #looms# were moving.
  : I stopped the nearest #hand# and dried the #floor# before anyone carried a #bolt# across.
  ask : Was anyone hurt?
  b : A small stop saved a fall.
  : Only our schedule lost a moment.

story river_bend [topic=pastimes self.age>=18]
  : I moved an #eel# #trap# to a quieter bend after the #market# closed.
  : The #river# was high, but the #bank# held beneath my feet.
  b : You know that stretch well. Any luck with it?
  : Enough to bring something fresh to the #table#.

story apple_order [topic=prices self.age>=18]
  : A #buyer# asked for a lower #price# while I was giving out #apples#.
  : I showed the #sample#, the #wagon# #cost#, and the #wages# written beside the #order#.
  ask : Did they agree?
  b : Clear numbers help.
  : We found a #bolt# that suited the #coin# they had.

rule @bark_door
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Leave the #doorway# clear. | I can see that #wagon# from here.

rule @bark_floor
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The #floor# is wet by the #beam#. | Put a dry #rag# over that #plank#.

rule @bark_apple
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Have a crisp #apple# before we count. | The #basket# is full today.

rule @bark_book
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say One #bolt# is missing its #mark#. | The #book# needs a new #page#.

rule @bark_shuttle
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say Keep a spare #shuttle# close. | That #warp# sounds slack.

rule @bark_road
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 12h
say The #wagon# has passed the #gate#. | I hope that #load# is complete.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I am checking the #orders# from my #desk#. | #greet#. Take an #apple# and tell me your business.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : I remember the #bolt# you asked about. | The #wagon# is still unloading on your return.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The #looms# have stopped; is this urgent? | I am upstairs now. Speak from the #door#.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : We can speak from either side of this #desk#. | State your need while the #door# stays open.
dlg @1 resident.job : I direct the #looms# at #self.workplace# and inspect each #bolt#. | The #hands#, #orders#, and #wagons# all need a fair count.
dlg @2 resident.job [self.working=yes] : I am matching #stock# to the #book#. | This #sample# needs my final #mark#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I will close the #shed# #door#. | #saying.capitalize#. Watch the #floor#.
dlg @2 resident.bye [here.time=night] : Good night. The #gate# is quiet now. | Go carefully along the #road#.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : #greet#. The #linen# #samples# are beside the #counter#. | I can show you a #bolt# and its posted #price#.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : There is no finished #linen# on the #shelf# today. | The next #wagon# may bring #stock#; I can hear what you offer.
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : Mm... the #looms# can wait for #morning#... | Come back when the #shed# opens.
dlg @4 shop.greet [here.shop=open topic.meeting=known] : Back for the #sample# we discussed? | I remember your #order#; the #bolt# is ready.
dlg @5 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare here.shop!=asleep] : #greet#. Ask me which #bolts# are ready. | I can show you the #samples# at this #counter#.
dlg @1 shop.prices [here.shop=open|bare] : The #price# sits beside each #sample#. | I will show the #cloth# and explain the #wagon# #cost#.
dlg @1 shop.bye : #farewell#. Keep the #linen# dry on the #road#. | #shop_bye# I have another #order# to mark.
dlg @1 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : Begin by winding a straight #warp#. | I will show how the #shuttle# should sound.
dlg @2 master.learn [here.teaches=yes topic.meeting=known] : You came back for another #lesson#. | Your last #knot# held; let us try the #beam#.
dlg @3 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : Stand beside the slow #loom# and watch my #hands#. | This #thread# needs even tension before you begin.
dlg @4 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : Take the spare #shuttle# and make one careful pass. | I will check the #weft# when you finish.
graft resident.hub
choice How do you run the looms? -> looms
node looms
say I assign a #hand# to each #loom#, compare the #bolts# with the #book#, and inspect any #flaw# before sale.
free
choice Why face the doorway? -> door
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node door
say From this #chair# I can see arriving #wagons# and hear anyone entering the #shed#. It keeps the #work# moving.
choice Back to the orders. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice May I inspect the linen? -> sample
node sample
say Of course. Feel the #edge# of this #sample# and look along the #weft#. I mark any #flaw# before setting a #price#.
free
choice What makes it cost this much? -> price
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node price
say The #thread#, the #hands#, the #wagon# #cost#, and the #gate# #toll# all appear in my #book#.
choice Back to the linen. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #looms# are working steadily. | #greet#. I have an #apple# on my #desk#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will finish the #book# tonight. | The #doorway# must stay clear for the last #hand#.
